; Fleet clj-kondo config — copied byte-identical to
; .clj-kondo/config.edn in each adopted repo (see cljfmt.edn header
; for the sync law). v1 pins the tool floor and otherwise runs the
; clj-kondo DEFAULT linter levels: the Phase 1 census measures the
; default gate. Linter levels are never demoted to make a repo pass;
; off-by-default idiom linters are enabled in deliberate fleet-wide
; batches, recorded here.
{:min-clj-kondo-version "2026.10.26"
 ;; ── eve.db.ds repo exception (sync-law named exception, see STATUS) ──
 ;; Eve ships no clj-kondo exports, so kondo cannot see that
 ;; eve.alpha/deftype (used as `eve/deftype`) and eve.deftype/deftype
 ;; are structurally clojure.core/deftype: a name, a field vector,
 ;; then protocol specs whose bodies close over the fields. Without
 ;; this mapping every field reference reads as an unresolved symbol
 ;; and every protocol method as an invalid arity. Same exception as
 ;; narcis (Phase 1 RETRO item 1); proposed upstream homes: Eve ships
 ;; clj-kondo exports for its macros, or the fleet template gains
 ;; this mapping for Eve-consuming repos.
 :lint-as {eve.alpha/deftype clojure.core/deftype
           eve.deftype/deftype clojure.core/deftype}}
